<!-- ============================================================
       FAQs
  ============================================================ -->
  <section class="sec">
  <div class="container sec-white">

    <div class="row justify-content-center p-5">

      <div class="col-12 col-md-6">
        <h2 class="zin-h2">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="col-12 col-md-6">
            <div class="accordion" id="zinFaq">
              <div class="faq-item">
                <button class="faq-btn" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq1" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq1">
                  Can't I just use Notion or Apple Notes?
                  <span class="faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true">▾</span>
                </button>
                <div id="faq1" class="collapse" data-bs-parent="#zinFaq">
                  <p class="faq-answer">You can. But general tools were not built for this job. They have no way to mine your past writing, no reading mode, and no structured way to use what you have captured. Most people do not maintain them with enough consistency to get real value from them.</p>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="faq-item">
                <button class="faq-btn" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq2" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq2">
                  I don't have anything worth capturing.
                  <span class="faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true">▾</span>
                </button>
                <div id="faq2" class="collapse" data-bs-parent="#zinFaq">
                  <p class="faq-answer">You almost certainly do. Your past writing alone contains more than you think — emails that said something true, documents with ideas you have since forgotten, conversations that shifted how you see something. The mining prompt surfaces more than most people expect. And if you are living and working, new material is arriving every day.</p>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="faq-item">
                <button class="faq-btn" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq3" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq3">
                  Is this another system I'll abandon?
                  <span class="faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true">▾</span>
                </button>
                <div id="faq3" class="collapse" data-bs-parent="#zinFaq">
                  <p class="faq-answer">Zin is designed to be minimal. Capture takes seconds. There is no maintenance overhead. It gets more useful the longer you use it, without ever becoming a project in itself.</p>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="faq-item">
                <button class="faq-btn" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq4" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq4">
                  Do I have time for this?
                  <span class="faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true">▾</span>
                </button>
                <div id="faq4" class="collapse" data-bs-parent="#zinFaq">
                  <p class="faq-answer">The bootstrap takes one session. Daily capture is two to five minutes. You save that time back the first time you need to retrieve something you would otherwise have lost.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>